<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    What Android's backup takes of MilO's files, and what it leaves. Two cases, with different
    rules: a backup to Shawn's Google account ("cloud-backup"), and a direct transfer from one
    phone to another when a new phone is set up ("device-transfer").

    EXCLUDE ELEMENTS ONLY. With no include element Android takes everything of the app that
    is not excluded here; a single include element switches that default off and takes only
    what is included. That matters most for the main database: Room keeps its newest changes
    in a second file, milo.db-wal, until it moves them into milo.db. A rule that included
    "milo.db" by name would leave the -wal file behind, and every trip that was still in it
    would be missing after a restore. So nothing names the main database at all: it is taken
    because it is not excluded, together with its -wal file.

    What is taken, in both cases:
      databases/milo.db (+ -wal)   the trips, the sent reports and the event log
      files/datastore/             the settings (a DataStore file)

    What is never taken, in either case:
      - no_backup/                 Android never takes this folder. It holds the crash files,
                                   MilO's copy of a chosen trip-start sound, the notes of the
                                   backup agent, the safety copies before an import and a file
                                   that is being imported. Each is about this phone, or too
                                   large for the cloud's 25 MB.
      - cache/                     Android never takes it either: the report files, and the
                                   event log as a text file.
      - the -shm and .lck files beside each database, below. Both are working files of one
        running process: SQLite builds the -shm file again from the -wal file when a database
        is opened, and the .lck file is Room's own lock. Neither holds data.
      - files/profileInstalled     written by Android's profile installer about this install.

    The raw GPS points (databases/points.db) are the one difference between the two cases:

      cloud-backup     EXCLUDED. A fix every five seconds is some 25 to 60 MB a year, and the
                       cloud backup takes NOTHING AT ALL from an app whose files are over
                       25 MB, without a word to anyone. The points must never be what pushes
                       the trips out of the backup. All four files of the database are
                       excluded together: a -wal file restored beside a new, empty points.db
                       would be read as that database's own log and corrupt it.
      device-transfer  INCLUDED. A transfer has a limit of 2 GB, and a new phone should have
                       the tracks of the old one.

    The file names are those of data/MiloDatabase.kt and data/PointsDatabase.kt. A database
    that is renamed there has to be renamed here.

    The device_ domains (device-protected storage, readable before the first unlock after a
    reboot) are not listed: MilO stores nothing there.

    No disableIfNoEncryptionCapabilities: with it, a phone without a screen lock would not be
    backed up at all, and Android says nothing about that either. With a screen lock set, the
    cloud backup is encrypted with it in any case.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="database" path="points.db" />
        <exclude domain="database" path="points.db-wal" />
        <exclude domain="database" path="points.db-shm" />
        <exclude domain="database" path="points.db.lck" />
        <exclude domain="database" path="milo.db-shm" />
        <exclude domain="database" path="milo.db.lck" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="profileInstalled" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="database" path="points.db-shm" />
        <exclude domain="database" path="points.db.lck" />
        <exclude domain="database" path="milo.db-shm" />
        <exclude domain="database" path="milo.db.lck" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="profileInstalled" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
